        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" ezremote:id="2468" ezremote:identifier="body" name="Body" type="ezxmltext">
          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/">
            <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">
              <embed size="original" view="embed" align="center" object_remote_id="ezdemo-img-blog-release"/>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph>Today we are releasing Exponential 6.0.15, the most complete release of the 6.0 line so far. It runs on PHP 8.1 to 8.5, ships front-end editing with expwt, modern designs with dark mode and a strict Content Security Policy, and installs a working site in under a minute.</paragraph>
            <section>
              <section>
                <header>Highlights</header>
                <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">
                  <ul>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/"><strong>expwt</strong>, the new website toolbar, replaces the old toolbar on every design.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/"><strong>Passkeys and two-factor sign-in</strong> for every account.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/"><strong>Velocity</strong>, the PHP application server, is the recommended way to run a site.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/"><strong>Site packages</strong> that install on SQLite, MySQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB and Oracle.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </paragraph>
              </section>
              <section>
                <header>Upgrading</header>
                <paragraph>Sites on 6.0.14 upgrade with the usual steps: update the code, run the upgrade scripts and clear the caches. The documentation has a full upgrade guide.</paragraph>
              </section>
            </section>
          </section>
